## Part II: Knowledge Representation

### Four-Layer Cortical Hierarchy

Inspired by visual cortex (V1→V2→V4→IT):

| Layer | Name | Analogy | Content | Purpose |
|-------|------|---------|---------|---------|
| **0** | TOKENS | V1 (edge detection) | Individual words | Atomic units |
| **1** | BIGRAMS | V2 (pattern detection) | Word pairs | Local structure |
| **2** | CONCEPTS | V4 (shape detection) | Semantic clusters | Emergent meaning |
| **3** | DOCUMENTS | IT (object recognition) | Full documents | Holistic view |

### Minicolumn — The Core Data Structure

**Location:** `cortical/minicolumn.py`

A neuron-inspired node in the knowledge graph with **four connection types**:

```python
minicolumn.lateral_connections      # Dict[str, float] — Within-layer
minicolumn.typed_connections        # Dict[str, Edge]  — Semantic edges
minicolumn.feedforward_connections  # Dict[str, float] — Upward (part→whole)
minicolumn.feedback_connections     # Dict[str, float] — Downward (whole→part)
```

### Semantic Relations

Relations between terms have typed weights:

| Relation | Weight | Example |
|----------|--------|---------|
| `IsA` | 1.5 | "dog IsA animal" |
| `SimilarTo` | 1.4 | "dog SimilarTo cat" |
| `PartOf` | 1.3 | "wheel PartOf car" |
| `DerivedFrom` | 1.2 | "quickly DerivedFrom quick" |
| `HasProperty` | 1.2 | "dog HasProperty loyal" |
| `Causes` | 1.1 | "rain Causes floods" |
| `RelatedTo` | 1.0 | Default co-occurrence |
| `CoOccurs` | 0.8 | Statistical co-occurrence |
| `Antonym` | 0.3 | "big Antonym small" (penalized) |

